  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WCO -Anti-corruption and integrity promotion (A-CIP) program for customs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A programme to improve governance and integrity in customs for selected WCO member countries, which, in turn, will improve revenue collection for domestic resource mobilization as well as improve the business environment for cross-border trade. The following countries are or have been involved in the bilateral component of the programme: Burkina Faso, Cote d&#x2019;Ivoire, Ethiopia, Ghana, Jordan, Liberia, Mali, Malawi, Mozambique, Nepal, Niger, Palestine, Sierra Leone, Tanzania and Tunisia.</narrative>
  </description>
